{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 40,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover, the LORD answered Job, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall he that contendeth with the Almighty instruct ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? he that reproveth God, let him answer it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Job answered the LORD, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I am vile; what shall I answer thee? I will lay my hand upon my mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Once have I spoken; but I will not answer: yes, twice; but I will proceed no further.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Gird up thy loins now like a man: I will demand of thee, and declare thou to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wilt thou also disannul my judgment? wilt thou condemn me, that thou mayest be righteous?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou an arm like God? or canst thou thunder with a voice like his?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Deck thyself now ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " majesty and excellence; and array thyself with glory and beauty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Cast abroad the rage of thy wrath: and behold every one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " proud, and abase him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Look on every one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " proud, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bring him low; and tread down the wicked in their place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hide them in the dust together; bind their faces in secret.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then will I also confess to thee that thy own right hand can save thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold now behemoth, which I made with thee; he eateth grass as an ox.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo now, his strength ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in his loins, and his force ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the navel of his belly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He moveth his tail like a cedar: the sinews of his male organs are wrapped together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His bones ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strong pieces of brass; his bones ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like bars of iron.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the chief of the ways of God: he that made him can make his sword to approach ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely the mountains bring him forth food, where all the beasts of the field play.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He lieth under the shady trees, in the covert of the reed, and fens.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The shady trees cover him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their shadow; the willows of the brook encompass him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, he drinketh up a river, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hasteth not: he trusteth that he can draw up Jordan into his mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.40.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.40.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He taketh it with his eyes: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " nose pierceth through snares.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
